# 🔴 No Reckless File Deletion

## 🚫 Never Delete When

- Don't understand file purpose
- References found
- Uncertain of impact scope
- User consent not obtained

## ✅ Correct Deletion Process (5 Steps)

1. **Identify Purpose**: Understand what the file does
2. **Search References**: Grep search all references
3. **Assess Impact**: Analyze deletion impact
4. **Provide Reason**: Explain why deletion is needed
5. **Obtain Consent**: Use AskQuestion to request confirmation

## Mandatory Pre-Deletion Checklist

- [ ] Searched all references (grep/rg)
- [ ] Viewed git history (git log --follow)
- [ ] Understand what this file does
- [ ] Assessed deletion impact
- [ ] Obtained user consent via AskQuestion

## File Deletion Risk Levels

| Risk Level | File Type | Handling |
|-----------|-----------|----------|
| 🔴 High | Core logic, configs, scripts | Must deep assess + user confirm |
| 🟡 Medium | Utilities, auxiliary files | Search references + user confirm |
| 🟢 Low | Temp files, logs | Confirm no references + user confirm |

**Core Mantra: Don't delete if don't understand, don't delete if referenced, don't delete if uncertain, don't delete without permission.**
